IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Fair Entitlements Guarantee Act 2012 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- what the former employee of an insolvent or
-- bankrupt employer meets: what counts as wages (s 7) and the 13-week wages entitlement period (s 5); whether I am
-- eligible for an advance (s 10) and the exclusions (ss 11, 12, 13); by when I must claim and whether my claim is
-- effective (s 14); how much the advance is (Part 3: ss 16 to 27, with the reductions in ss 17 and 18); review of the
-- Secretary's decision (ss 38, 40, 41); and what I must repay if I am paid later from somewhere else (s 34).
--
-- SEAT: the former employee. "My employer went into liquidation owing me wages, leave and redundancy pay. Can I claim
-- under the Fair Entitlements Guarantee, by when, and how much will I get?" The Act is addressed to the Secretary; its
-- provisions are encoded as what they mean for that person: when the Secretary must find me eligible, what the
-- Secretary must pay, what the Secretary may take off, and what I can do about the decision.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 5, compilation date 21 February 2025 (register id C2025C00164), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2012A00159.txt.
--
-- THE MAXIMUM WEEKLY WAGE IS AN INPUT. s 5 sets it at $2,364.00 "or the result of indexation ... in accordance with the
-- regulations". The Fair Entitlements Guarantee Regulations 2012 are not deposited, so the current figure is asked for.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Employment for a partnership by two or more partners (ss 10(2), 11(3), 12(2), 25(3), 33), and an employer
-- in administration under a Minister's s 49 declaration, answer `not covered`. Section 25 (recently agreed changes in
-- terms: the person states the entitlement under the unchanged terms where the Secretary applies it); costs of the
-- winding up or bankruptcy (ss 20 to 23: the person states the entitlement less any such cost); payment and instalments
-- (s 28); recovery through the winding up (ss 29 to 33); the Secretary's own-initiative review (s 37); information
-- (Part 6 Division 3); s 50 (schemes for contractors, by regulation); s 9A, s 51 to s 55; delegations.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Fair Entitlements Guarantee Act 2012 -- the former employee's questions`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

-- The stable l4 has no REFUSE. A question that can reach a gap answers with an `Answer`: either `answered` with the
-- value, or `not covered` with the reason.
DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- ss 10(2), 11(3), 12(2), 25(3), 33
    `employment for a partnership by two or more of the partners is not encoded (s 10(2))`
    -- s 49
    `an employer in administration under a Minister's declaration under s 49 is not encoded`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `s 7 -- does this payment count as wages`

-- s 7(1): "Wages includes the following: (a) allowances; (b) loadings; (c) amounts payable for overtime; (d) amounts
-- payable at penalty rates; (e) other amounts that the governing instrument for the relevant employment identifies
-- separately and makes payable regularly." (2): "However, the following are not wages: (a) discretionary payments (such
-- as bonuses); (b) reimbursements; (c) payments of expenses relating to travel or relocation." (3): "Amounts that are not
-- payable on an ongoing basis are not wages, unless they are amounts described in subsection (1)."
-- Ordinary pay for work done is wages in the ordinary meaning, which s 7 extends ("includes") rather than replaces.
DECLARE `Kind of payment` IS ONE OF
    `ordinary pay for work done or paid leave taken`
    `an allowance`
    `a loading`
    `overtime`
    `penalty rates`
    `another amount my award or agreement identifies separately and makes payable regularly`
    `a discretionary payment, such as a bonus`
    `a reimbursement`
    `a payment of travel or relocation expenses`
    `another amount that is not payable on an ongoing basis`

@export Does this payment from my employer count as "wages" under the Fair Entitlements Guarantee (s 7)?
GIVEN `the payment` IS A `Kind of payment` @desc What kind of payment it is, as your award, agreement or contract describes it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this payment wages` IF
    CONSIDER `the payment`
    WHEN `a discretionary payment, such as a bonus` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a reimbursement` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a payment of travel or relocation expenses` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `another amount that is not payable on an ongoing basis` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 5 -- the wages entitlement period`

-- s 5: "wages entitlement period for a person whose employment by an employer has ended means the 13 weeks ending at the
-- earlier of the following times (or either of those times if they are the same): (a) the time the person's employment
-- ended; (b) the first time an insolvency practitioner (other than a restructuring practitioner ...) has power (however
-- expressed) to control or manage employment by ... the employer". Thirteen weeks are 91 days; counted in whole days
-- ending on the day of the earlier event, they begin 90 days before it (NOTES.md finding 3).
DECLARE `Period` HAS
    `first day` IS A DATE
    `last day`  IS A DATE

GIVEN `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE
      `an insolvency practitioner took control of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the practitioner took control` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the wages entitlement period` MEANS
    IF     `an insolvency practitioner took control of employment`
       AND `the day the practitioner took control` LESS THAN `the day my employment ended`
    THEN `the day the practitioner took control`
    ELSE `the day my employment ended`

@export Which 13 weeks of unpaid wages does the Fair Entitlements Guarantee cover (the wages entitlement period, s 5)?
GIVEN `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE @desc The day your employment with the insolvent employer ended
      `an insolvency practitioner took control of employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a liquidator, administrator, receiver, bankruptcy trustee or other insolvency practitioner (not a restructuring practitioner) had power to control or manage your employer's employees before or when your employment ended
      `the day the practitioner took control` IS A DATE @desc The first day that insolvency practitioner had that power (ignored if none did)
GIVETH A `Period`
`What is my wages entitlement period` MEANS
    `Period` WITH
        `first day` IS `the last day` MINUS 90
        `last day`  IS `the last day`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `the end of the wages entitlement period` `the day my employment ended` `an insolvency practitioner took control of employment` `the day the practitioner took control`

§§ `ss 10 to 13 -- am I eligible for an advance`

-- s 5: "insolvency event: an insolvency event happens to an employer of a person: (a) when a liquidator of the employer
-- is appointed (provisionally or otherwise) under the Corporations Act 2001; or (b) when the employer becomes a bankrupt
-- under the Bankruptcy Act 1966". Paragraph (c) (a partnership) is not covered. s 49: an administration under Part 5.3A
-- counts only under a Minister's declaration, not covered.
DECLARE `What happened to my employer` IS ONE OF
    `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise`
    `my employer became a bankrupt`
    `my employer is in administration and the Minister has declared under s 49 that the Act applies`
    `none of these`

-- s 10(1)(g): "an Australian citizen or, under the Migration Act 1958, the holder of a permanent visa or a special
-- category visa". The visa classes are borrowed terms, asked as facts.
DECLARE `My status when my employment ended` IS ONE OF
    `an Australian citizen`
    `the holder of a permanent visa`
    `the holder of a special category visa`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `Am I eligible` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I am eligible for an advance (s 10(1)), if the Secretary is satisfied of the facts I have given`
    `no: my employment has not ended (s 10(1)(a))`
    `no: no insolvency event (a liquidator's appointment or my employer's bankruptcy) has happened on or after 5 December 2012 (s 10(1)(b))`
    `no: my employment did not end because of the insolvency, nor less than 6 months before or after an insolvency practitioner was appointed (s 10(1)(c))`
    `no: I am not owed wages, annual leave, long service leave, notice or redundancy pay (s 10(1)(d))`
    `no: I have not taken reasonable steps to prove my debts in the winding up or bankruptcy (s 10(1)(e))`
    `no: I did not take reasonable steps, before the insolvency event, to be paid what I was already owed (s 10(1)(f))`
    `no: when my employment ended I was not an Australian citizen or the holder of a permanent or special category visa (s 10(1)(g))`
    `no: I have not made an effective claim (s 10(1)(h), s 14)`
    `no: I am excluded as an excluded employee, a relative or a recent spouse or de facto partner of my employer (s 11)`
    `no: I am excluded as newly employed after working for my employer as a contractor (s 12)`
    `no: my employer was within the Special Employee Entitlements Scheme for Ansett Group Employees (s 13)`

-- s 10(1)(b): the event happened "after the commencement of this section". Section 10 commenced on 5 December 2012
-- (s 2, table item 2).
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened to my employer`
      `the day it happened` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an insolvency event happened after the commencement` IF
        (    `what happened` EQUALS `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise`
         OR  `what happened` EQUALS `my employer became a bankrupt`)
    AND `the day it happened` AT LEAST (Date 5 12 2012)

-- s 10(1)(c): "the end of the employment: (i) was due to the insolvency of the employer; or (ii) occurred less than 6
-- months before the appointment of an insolvency practitioner for the employer; or (iii) occurred on or after the
-- appointment of an insolvency practitioner for the employer". (ii) and (iii) together: the end was later than the day
-- 6 months before the appointment. Exactly 6 months before is not "less than 6 months before".
GIVEN `my employment ended because my employer was insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE
      `the day an insolvency practitioner was first appointed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the end of my employment is connected with the insolvency` IF
        `my employment ended because my employer was insolvent`
    OR  `the day my employment ended` GREATER THAN (`add months` `the day an insolvency practitioner was first appointed` (-6))

-- s 11(1): not eligible if "section 556 of the Corporations Act 2001 applies to the winding up of the employer" and "the
-- person is an excluded employee under that section" (a director, or a relative of a director, in the 12 months before;
-- a borrowed term, asked as a fact). (2): for a bankrupt employer, not eligible if "(a) the person is a relative (as
-- defined in the Corporations Act 2001) of the employer; or (b) the person was a spouse or de facto partner ... of the
-- employer at any time within the 12 months ending on the date of the bankruptcy".
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened to my employer`
      `I am an excluded employee under s 556 of the Corporations Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a relative of my bankrupt employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was my bankrupt employer's spouse or de facto partner in the 12 months before the bankruptcy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am excluded for a personal connection with my employer` IF
        (    `what happened` EQUALS `a liquidator was appointed, provisionally or otherwise`
         AND `I am an excluded employee under s 556 of the Corporations Act`)
    OR  (    `what happened` EQUALS `my employer became a bankrupt`
         AND (`I am a relative of my bankrupt employer` OR `I was my bankrupt employer's spouse or de facto partner in the 12 months before the bankruptcy`))

-- s 12(1): not eligible "if the Secretary is satisfied that all the following apply: (a) the person started to be
-- employed by the employer in the 6 months ending at the earlier of ... (i) the end of the employment; (ii) the
-- appointment of an insolvency practitioner for the employer; (b) the person was engaged by the employer, but not as an
-- employee of the employer, before the start of the employment; (c) it was reasonable to expect at the start of that
-- employment that the employer would not be able to meet the employer's obligations". The Secretary's satisfaction on
-- (c) is asked as a fact.
GIVEN `the day I started` IS A DATE
      `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE
      `the day an insolvency practitioner was first appointed` IS A DATE
      `I worked for my employer as a contractor before I became its employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary is satisfied it was reasonable to expect my employer could not meet its obligations to me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am excluded as newly employed after working as a contractor` IF
        `the day I started` GREATER THAN (`add months` `the earlier event` (-6))
    AND `the day I started` AT MOST `the earlier event`
    AND `I worked for my employer as a contractor before I became its employee`
    AND `the Secretary is satisfied it was reasonable to expect my employer could not meet its obligations to me`
    WHERE
        `the earlier event` MEANS IF `the day my employment ended` AT MOST `the day an insolvency practitioner was first appointed` THEN `the day my employment ended` ELSE `the day an insolvency practitioner was first appointed`

GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened to my employer`
      `the day it happened` IS A DATE
      `my employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE
      `the day I started` IS A DATE
      `the day an insolvency practitioner was first appointed` IS A DATE
      `ended because insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `owed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `owed before the event` IS A BOOLEAN
      `chased before the event` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my status` IS A `My status when my employment ended`
      `claimed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 556 excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `relative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `contractor first` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Secretary satisfied under s 12(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Ansett` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Am I eligible`
`my eligibility` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `my employment has ended`) THEN `no: my employment has not ended (s 10(1)(a))`
        IF (NOT `an insolvency event happened after the commencement` `what happened` `the day it happened`)
            THEN `no: no insolvency event (a liquidator's appointment or my employer's bankruptcy) has happened on or after 5 December 2012 (s 10(1)(b))`
        IF (NOT `the end of my employment is connected with the insolvency` `ended because insolvent` `the day my employment ended` `the day an insolvency practitioner was first appointed`)
            THEN `no: my employment did not end because of the insolvency, nor less than 6 months before or after an insolvency practitioner was appointed (s 10(1)(c))`
        IF (NOT `owed`) THEN `no: I am not owed wages, annual leave, long service leave, notice or redundancy pay (s 10(1)(d))`
        IF (NOT `proved`) THEN `no: I have not taken reasonable steps to prove my debts in the winding up or bankruptcy (s 10(1)(e))`
        IF `owed before the event` AND (NOT `chased before the event`)
            THEN `no: I did not take reasonable steps, before the insolvency event, to be paid what I was already owed (s 10(1)(f))`
        IF `my status` EQUALS `none of these`
            THEN `no: when my employment ended I was not an Australian citizen or the holder of a permanent or special category visa (s 10(1)(g))`
        IF (NOT `claimed`) THEN `no: I have not made an effective claim (s 10(1)(h), s 14)`
        IF `I am excluded for a personal connection with my employer` `what happened` `s 556 excluded` `relative` `spouse`
            THEN `no: I am excluded as an excluded employee, a relative or a recent spouse or de facto partner of my employer (s 11)`
        IF `I am excluded as newly employed after working as a contractor` `the day I started` `the day my employment ended` `the day an insolvency practitioner was first appointed` `contractor first` `Secretary satisfied under s 12(1)(c)`
            THEN `no: I am excluded as newly employed after working for my employer as a contractor (s 12)`
        IF `Ansett` THEN `no: my employer was within the Special Employee Entitlements Scheme for Ansett Group Employees (s 13)`
        OTHERWISE `yes: I am eligible for an advance (s 10(1)), if the Secretary is satisfied of the facts I have given`

@export Am I eligible for a Fair Entitlements Guarantee advance for the wages and entitlements my insolvent employer owes me (ss 10 to 13)?
GIVEN `I was employed for a partnership by two or more partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer was a partnership, with two or more of the partners employing you (not encoded)
      `what happened to my employer` IS A `What happened to my employer` @desc What has happened to your employer: a liquidator appointed (including a provisional liquidator), the employer (a person) made bankrupt, an administration covered by a Minister's s 49 declaration, or none of these (an administration or receivership alone is not enough)
      `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc The day the liquidator was appointed or your employer became bankrupt
      `my employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment with this employer has ended
      `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE @desc The day your employment ended
      `the day I started` IS A DATE @desc The day you started as this employer's employee
      `the day an insolvency practitioner was first appointed` IS A DATE @desc The day the first insolvency practitioner (administrator, liquidator, receiver, restructuring practitioner, bankruptcy trustee or a secured creditor taking control of property) was appointed for your employer
      `my employment ended because my employer was insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment ended because your employer was insolvent
      `I am owed wages, leave, notice or redundancy pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer still owes you, wholly or partly, unpaid wages, annual leave, long service leave, pay in lieu of notice or redundancy pay
      `I have taken reasonable steps to prove those debts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have taken reasonable steps to prove those debts in the winding up or bankruptcy, such as lodging a proof of debt with the liquidator or trustee
      `I was owed some of it before the insolvency event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any of what you are owed was already owing before the liquidator was appointed or your employer became bankrupt
      `I took reasonable steps before then to be paid it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before that event, you took reasonable steps to be paid what was already owing (ignored if nothing was)
      `my status when my employment ended` IS A `My status when my employment ended` @desc Whether, when your employment ended, you were an Australian citizen, a permanent visa holder, a special category visa holder (a New Zealand citizen in Australia), or none of these
      `I have made an effective claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made a claim to the Secretary on the approved form, with the documents asked for, in time (see the question on claiming)
      `I am an excluded employee under s 556 of the Corporations Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an "excluded employee" in the winding up under s 556 of the Corporations Act 2001 (in the 12 months before, a director of the company, or a director's spouse or relative)
      `I am a relative of my bankrupt employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your employer is a bankrupt person: whether you are their relative, as the Corporations Act 2001 defines it
      `I was my bankrupt employer's spouse or de facto partner in the 12 months before the bankruptcy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your employer is a bankrupt person: whether you were their spouse or de facto partner at any time in the 12 months ending on the date of the bankruptcy
      `I worked for my employer as a contractor before I became its employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before you became its employee, this employer engaged you otherwise than as an employee (for example as a contractor)
      `the Secretary is satisfied it was reasonable to expect my employer could not meet its obligations to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary is satisfied that, when you started as an employee, it was reasonable to expect your employer could not meet its obligations to you for the whole of your employment (the Secretary's judgment)
      `my employer was in the Ansett scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer was within the Special Employee Entitlements Scheme for Ansett Group Employees
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Am I eligible`
`Am I eligible for an advance` MEANS
    IF `I was employed for a partnership by two or more partners`
    THEN `not covered` `employment for a partnership by two or more of the partners is not encoded (s 10(2))`
    ELSE IF `what happened to my employer` EQUALS `my employer is in administration and the Minister has declared under s 49 that the Act applies`
         THEN `not covered` `an employer in administration under a Minister's declaration under s 49 is not encoded`
         ELSE `answered` (`my eligibility` `what happened to my employer` `the day it happened` `my employment has ended` `the day my employment ended` `the day I started` `the day an insolvency practitioner was first appointed` `my employment ended because my employer was insolvent` `I am owed wages, leave, notice or redundancy pay` `I have taken reasonable steps to prove those debts` `I was owed some of it before the insolvency event` `I took reasonable steps before then to be paid it` `my status when my employment ended` `I have made an effective claim` `I am an excluded employee under s 556 of the Corporations Act` `I am a relative of my bankrupt employer` `I was my bankrupt employer's spouse or de facto partner in the 12 months before the bankruptcy` `I worked for my employer as a contractor before I became its employee` `the Secretary is satisfied it was reasonable to expect my employer could not meet its obligations to me` `my employer was in the Ansett scheme`)

§§ `s 14 -- by when must I claim, and is my claim effective`

-- s 14(2): "The claim must be made before the end of 12 months after the later of the following events: (a) an insolvency
-- event happens to the employer; (b) the person's employment by the employer ends." The 12 months after a day begin the
-- next day, so they end on the same date a year on (`add months` clamps 29 February to 28 February).
-- (3): "However, if the employer is or was a bankrupt, the claim must be or have been made before the discharge of the
-- employer's bankruptcy." Read here as: the last whole day is the day before the discharge (NOTES.md finding 4).
GIVEN `the day of the insolvency event` IS A DATE
      `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE
      `my employer is a bankrupt who has been, or will be, discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the discharge` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to claim` MEANS
    IF     `my employer is a bankrupt who has been, or will be, discharged`
       AND (`the day of the discharge` MINUS 1) LESS THAN `the end of the 12 months`
    THEN `the day of the discharge` MINUS 1
    ELSE `the end of the 12 months`
    WHERE
        `the end of the 12 months` MEANS `add months` `the later event` 12
        `the later event` MEANS IF `the day of the insolvency event` AT LEAST `the day my employment ended` THEN `the day of the insolvency event` ELSE `the day my employment ended`

@export By what day must I make my Fair Entitlements Guarantee claim (s 14(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the day of the insolvency event` IS A DATE @desc The day the liquidator was appointed or your employer became bankrupt
      `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE @desc The day your employment ended
      `my employer is a bankrupt who has been, or will be, discharged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your employer is a bankrupt person: whether you know the day the bankruptcy was, or will be, discharged
      `the day of the discharge` IS A DATE @desc The day of that discharge (ignored if not)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I claim` MEANS
    `the last day to claim` `the day of the insolvency event` `the day my employment ended` `my employer is a bankrupt who has been, or will be, discharged` `the day of the discharge`

-- s 14(1): "To be effective ..., a claim ... must: (a) be in a form approved by the Secretary; and (b) be accompanied by
-- any documents required by the Secretary; and (c) be made in accordance with subsection (2), and with subsection (3)
-- if it applies." (4): it "is not effective ... if it is made after a claim ... was made for a payment, under the scheme
-- known as the General Employee Entitlements and Redundancy Scheme, connected with the person's employment by the
-- employer." (5): "Subsection (4) does not apply if the earlier claim was rejected because an insolvency event had not
-- happened to the employer before the commencement of this section."
@export Is my Fair Entitlements Guarantee claim effective (s 14)?
GIVEN `the day I claimed` IS A DATE @desc The day you made your claim to the Secretary
      `the day of the insolvency event` IS A DATE @desc The day the liquidator was appointed or your employer became bankrupt
      `the day my employment ended` IS A DATE @desc The day your employment ended
      `my employer is a bankrupt who has been, or will be, discharged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your employer is a bankrupt person: whether you know the day the bankruptcy was, or will be, discharged
      `the day of the discharge` IS A DATE @desc The day of that discharge (ignored if not)
      `I used the approved form with the documents asked for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you claimed on the form the Secretary approved, with every document the Secretary required
      `I claimed earlier under GEERS for this job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before this claim, you claimed for this employment under the General Employee Entitlements and Redundancy Scheme (GEERS)
      `GEERS rejected it because the insolvency was before 5 December 2012` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that GEERS claim was rejected because no insolvency event had happened to your employer before 5 December 2012 (ignored if you made none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim effective` IF
        `I used the approved form with the documents asked for`
    AND `the day I claimed` AT MOST (`the last day to claim` `the day of the insolvency event` `the day my employment ended` `my employer is a bankrupt who has been, or will be, discharged` `the day of the discharge`)
    AND (    (NOT `I claimed earlier under GEERS for this job`)
         OR  `GEERS rejected it because the insolvency was before 5 December 2012`)

§§ `Part 3 -- how much is my advance`

-- s 26(1), (2): if the governing instrument "provided for a rate of pay relevant to working out the basic amount that,
-- when expressed as a weekly rate, exceeded the maximum weekly wage rate at the end of the employment", the basic amount
-- is worked out "as if the governing instrument had provided for the relevant wage rate to be the maximum weekly wage
-- rate". Leave, notice and redundancy pay are a number of weeks at that rate, so the entitlement is scaled down by the
-- ratio of the two rates. One rate is asked for all four entitlements (NOTES.md finding 5).
GIVEN `my weekly rate` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum weekly wage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekly rate counted` MEANS min `my weekly rate` `the maximum weekly wage`

GIVEN `my weekly rate` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum weekly wage` IS A NUMBER
      `the entitlement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the entitlement at the rate counted (s 26)` MEANS
    IF   `my weekly rate` GREATER THAN `the maximum weekly wage`
    THEN `the entitlement` TIMES (`the maximum weekly wage` DIVIDED BY `my weekly rate`)
    ELSE `the entitlement`

-- s 19(1): reduce "the basic amount (but not below nil) by" (2) amounts attributable to the entitlement "paid by
-- anyone" to me (other than costs of the winding up) and (3) amounts "payable (and have not been paid) by anyone" other
-- than under the winding up, the bankruptcy or this Act. Asked as one figure per entitlement.
GIVEN `the basic amount` IS A NUMBER
      `paid or payable from elsewhere` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount for the entitlement (s 19)` MEANS max 0 (`the basic amount` MINUS `paid or payable from elsewhere`)

-- s 20, s 21: the basic amount for the annual leave and long service leave entitlements is "so much of the entitlement as
-- is not a cost of the winding up or bankruptcy of the employer" (the person states the entitlement without any such
-- cost); s 26 applies.
GIVEN `my weekly rate` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum weekly wage` IS A NUMBER
      `the entitlement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the basic amount for leave (ss 20, 21)` MEANS
    `the entitlement at the rate counted (s 26)` `my weekly rate` `the maximum weekly wage` `the entitlement`

-- s 22: the basic amount for the payment in lieu of notice entitlement is so much of it as "(b) does not exceed 5 weeks'
-- pay at the rate relevant to working out that entitlement"; s 26 applies, also to that limit.
GIVEN `my weekly rate` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum weekly wage` IS A NUMBER
      `the entitlement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the basic amount for notice (s 22)` MEANS
    min (`the entitlement at the rate counted (s 26)` `my weekly rate` `the maximum weekly wage` `the entitlement`)
        (5 TIMES (`the weekly rate counted` `my weekly rate` `the maximum weekly wage`))

-- s 23: the basic amount for the redundancy pay entitlement is so much of it as "(b) does not exceed the total of: (i) 4
-- weeks' pay ... for each full year of the person's service ... for which the employer was required to pay redundancy pay
-- by the governing instrument ...; and (ii) if that instrument requires payment of redundancy pay for a proportion of a
-- year ...--that proportion of 4 weeks' pay". The years are asked as one number, with a part year only where the
-- instrument pays for one; s 26 applies.
GIVEN `my weekly rate` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum weekly wage` IS A NUMBER
      `the entitlement` IS A NUMBER
      `the years of service counted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the basic amount for redundancy (s 23)` MEANS
    min (`the entitlement at the rate counted (s 26)` `my weekly rate` `the maximum weekly wage` `the entitlement`)
        ((4 TIMES (`the weekly rate counted` `my weekly rate` `the maximum weekly wage`)) TIMES `the years of service counted`)

-- s 27: the maximum weekly wage applies to the wages entitlement if (2) the instrument provided a rate for the work
-- envisaged to be done regularly that "when expressed as a weekly rate, exceeded the maximum weekly wage rate at the end
-- of that period"; or (3) it provided no such rate, or (4) the Secretary is satisfied there is no regular pattern of hours
-- or wages, and in either case "the person's average weekly wage for that period" -- "dividing the person's wages
-- entitlement by the number of weeks for which he or she was employed by the employer in that period" (5) -- "is greater
-- than the maximum weekly wage". (6): the basic amount is then worked out "as if the governing instrument ... had
-- entitled the person, for each of the weeks for which the employer employed the person in the wages entitlement period,
-- to wages at the maximum weekly wage rate".
-- s 24: "the wages entitlement less any amount required to be withheld under Part 2-5 (Pay as you go (PAYG) withholding)
-- in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953 from the wages covered by the entitlement" (asked as a figure).
GIVEN `the maximum weekly wage` IS A NUMBER
      `my wages entitlement` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks I was employed in the period` IS A NUMBER
      `my instrument set a rate for my regular work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that rate as a weekly rate` IS A NUMBER
      `the Secretary is satisfied there is no regular pattern` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the PAYG amount to be withheld` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the basic amount for wages (ss 24, 27)` MEANS
    max 0 (`the wages counted` MINUS `the PAYG amount to be withheld`)
    WHERE
        `the average weekly wage` MEANS
            IF `the weeks I was employed in the period` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN `my wages entitlement` DIVIDED BY `the weeks I was employed in the period`
            ELSE 0
        `s 27 applies` MEANS
                (    `my instrument set a rate for my regular work`
                 AND `that rate as a weekly rate` GREATER THAN `the maximum weekly wage`)
            OR  (    ((NOT `my instrument set a rate for my regular work`) OR `the Secretary is satisfied there is no regular pattern`)
                 AND `the average weekly wage` GREATER THAN `the maximum weekly wage`)
        `the wages counted` MEANS
            IF `s 27 applies`
            THEN `the weeks I was employed in the period` TIMES `the maximum weekly wage`
            ELSE `my wages entitlement`

-- s 16(2): leave out the notice and redundancy amounts if "(a) the business in which the employer employed the person is
-- transferred to someone else (the transferee) other than the bankruptcy trustee ...; and (b) within 14 days of the end
-- of the person's employment ..., the transferee offers to employ the person" in the same or substantially the same work
-- on terms no less favourable overall. (3): "taken never to have applied" if the transferee employs the person and then
-- ends the job as no longer required, or becomes insolvent and the employment ends in connection with it. (4): "does not
-- apply ... because of an insolvency event that happened to the employer on or after 1 July 2014".
GIVEN `the day of the insolvency event` IS A DATE
      `a buyer of the business offered me the same work on terms no less favourable within 14 days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer later made my job redundant or became insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `notice and redundancy are left out (s 16(2))` IF
        `the day of the insolvency event` LESS THAN (Date 1 7 2014)
    AND `a buyer of the business offered me the same work on terms no less favourable within 14 days`
    AND (NOT `the buyer later made my job redundant or became insolvent`)

@export How much is my Fair Entitlements Guarantee advance (Part 3, ss 16 to 27)?
GIVEN `I was employed for a partnership by two or more partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer was a partnership, with two or more of the partners employing you (not encoded)
      `the maximum weekly wage` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum weekly wage at the end of your employment, in dollars: $2,364 in the Act, indexed each year under the Fair Entitlements Guarantee Regulations 2012 (not encoded: supply the figure in force)
      `my weekly rate` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly rate of pay under your award, agreement or contract at the end of the employment, in dollars (the rate your leave, notice and redundancy pay are worked out at)
      `my unpaid annual leave` IS A NUMBER @desc What your award, agreement or contract entitles you to for annual leave accrued and not taken at the end of your employment, in dollars, before anything was paid towards it
      `my unpaid long service leave` IS A NUMBER @desc What you are entitled to for long service leave accrued (or pro rata) at the end of your employment, in dollars, before anything was paid towards it
      `my pay in lieu of notice` IS A NUMBER @desc What you are entitled to for a shortfall in your notice of termination, in dollars, before anything was paid towards it
      `my redundancy pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The redundancy pay you are entitled to, in dollars, before anything was paid towards it
      `the years of service my redundancy pay counts` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years of your service your redundancy pay is payable for: full years, plus a part year only if your award or agreement pays for part years
      `my wages entitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc Your wages (including allowances, loadings, overtime and penalty rates) for work done or paid leave taken in the 13-week wages entitlement period, in dollars, before tax and before anything was paid towards it
      `the weeks I was employed in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of that 13-week period you were employed (13 if all of it; need not be a whole number)
      `my instrument set a rate for my regular work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your award, agreement or contract set a rate of pay, at the end of that period, for work you were expected to do regularly
      `that rate as a weekly rate` IS A NUMBER @desc That rate expressed as a weekly rate, in dollars (ignored if none)
      `the Secretary is satisfied there is no regular pattern` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary is satisfied that there was no regular pattern of your hours, or of your wages, over the weeks of that period (the Secretary's judgment)
      `the PAYG amount to be withheld from those wages` IS A NUMBER @desc The tax that must be withheld under PAYG from the wages counted, in dollars
      `already paid or payable for annual leave` IS A NUMBER @desc What anyone has paid you (or someone for your benefit) for the annual leave, or must pay you outside the winding up or bankruptcy, in dollars
      `already paid or payable for long service leave` IS A NUMBER @desc The same, for long service leave, in dollars
      `already paid or payable for notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The same, for pay in lieu of notice, in dollars
      `already paid or payable for redundancy` IS A NUMBER @desc The same, for redundancy pay, in dollars
      `already paid or payable for wages` IS A NUMBER @desc The same, for the wages in the 13-week period, in dollars
      `the day of the insolvency event` IS A DATE @desc The day the liquidator was appointed or your employer became bankrupt
      `a buyer of the business offered me the same work on terms no less favourable within 14 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business was transferred (not to a bankruptcy trustee) and, within 14 days of your employment ending, the new owner offered you the same or substantially the same work on terms no less favourable overall
      `the buyer later made my job redundant or became insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that new owner then employed you and ended the job as no longer needed, or became insolvent and your job with them ended in connection with it
      `the Secretary has reduced it for my debts to my employer by` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount, in dollars, by which the Secretary has decided to reduce the advance because you owe your employer money (0 if none)
      `my debts to my employer` IS A NUMBER @desc The total you owe your employer, in dollars
      `the Secretary has reduced it to nil under s 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary, satisfied that the liquidator or trustee expects to have enough in the next 112 days to pay you in full, has reduced the advance to nil
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much is my advance` MEANS
    IF `I was employed for a partnership by two or more partners`
    THEN `not covered` `employment for a partnership by two or more of the partners is not encoded (s 10(2))`
    ELSE IF `the Secretary has reduced it to nil under s 18`
         THEN `answered` 0
         ELSE `answered` (max 0 (`the s 16 total` MINUS (min `the Secretary has reduced it for my debts to my employer by` `my debts to my employer`)))
    WHERE
        `annual leave` MEANS `the amount for the entitlement (s 19)` (`the basic amount for leave (ss 20, 21)` `my weekly rate` `the maximum weekly wage` `my unpaid annual leave`) `already paid or payable for annual leave`
        `long service leave` MEANS `the amount for the entitlement (s 19)` (`the basic amount for leave (ss 20, 21)` `my weekly rate` `the maximum weekly wage` `my unpaid long service leave`) `already paid or payable for long service leave`
        `notice` MEANS `the amount for the entitlement (s 19)` (`the basic amount for notice (s 22)` `my weekly rate` `the maximum weekly wage` `my pay in lieu of notice`) `already paid or payable for notice`
        `redundancy` MEANS `the amount for the entitlement (s 19)` (`the basic amount for redundancy (s 23)` `my weekly rate` `the maximum weekly wage` `my redundancy pay` `the years of service my redundancy pay counts`) `already paid or payable for redundancy`
        `wages` MEANS `the amount for the entitlement (s 19)` (`the basic amount for wages (ss 24, 27)` `the maximum weekly wage` `my wages entitlement` `the weeks I was employed in the period` `my instrument set a rate for my regular work` `that rate as a weekly rate` `the Secretary is satisfied there is no regular pattern` `the PAYG amount to be withheld from those wages`) `already paid or payable for wages`
        `the s 16 total` MEANS
            IF `notice and redundancy are left out (s 16(2))` `the day of the insolvency event` `a buyer of the business offered me the same work on terms no less favourable within 14 days` `the buyer later made my job redundant or became insolvent`
            THEN `annual leave` PLUS `long service leave` PLUS `wages`
            ELSE `annual leave` PLUS `long service leave` PLUS `notice` PLUS `redundancy` PLUS `wages`

§§ `ss 38, 40, 41 -- review of the Secretary's decision`

-- s 36: the Secretary must give me written notice of the decision on eligibility and on the amount, with reasons and my
-- review rights. s 38(1), (2): I "may apply to the Secretary for review" and the application "must be made within 28
-- days after the date of the notice of the decision, or such longer time as the Secretary allows." The day of the
-- notice is not counted.
@export By what day must I ask the Secretary to review the decision on my Fair Entitlements Guarantee claim (s 38(2))?
GIVEN `the date of the notice of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The date of the Secretary's written notice of the decision on your eligibility or on the amount of your advance
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply for review` MEANS `the date of the notice of the decision` PLUS 28

-- s 40(1): the Administrative Review Tribunal reviews "(a) a decision ... whether the person is eligible for an advance
-- that has been affirmed under Subdivision B or has been substituted under that Subdivision for an earlier decision; or
-- (b) a decision ... on the amount of an advance ... that has been affirmed or varied under Subdivision B or
-- substituted". So the Secretary's review under s 38 comes first. s 41: where the amount involved the s 17 reduction for
-- a debt owed to the employer, "(2) The Tribunal cannot review the exercise of that power".
DECLARE `Where I take the decision` IS ONE OF
    `first ask the Secretary to review it, within 28 days of the notice (s 38); the Tribunal reviews only the decision made on that review (s 40(1))`
    `I may apply to the Administrative Review Tribunal for review of the decision made on the Secretary's review (s 40(1))`
    `I may apply to the Administrative Review Tribunal, but it cannot review the Secretary's reduction for my debts to my employer (s 41)`

@export Can I take the decision on my Fair Entitlements Guarantee claim to the Administrative Review Tribunal (ss 38, 40, 41)?
GIVEN `the Secretary has reviewed it on my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied to the Secretary for review under s 38 and the Secretary has affirmed, varied or replaced the decision
      `what I dispute includes the reduction for my debts to my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you dispute includes the Secretary's reduction of your advance under s 17 because you owe your employer money
GIVETH A `Where I take the decision`
`Where can I take the decision` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Secretary has reviewed it on my application`)
    THEN `first ask the Secretary to review it, within 28 days of the notice (s 38); the Tribunal reviews only the decision made on that review (s 40(1))`
    ELSE IF `what I dispute includes the reduction for my debts to my employer`
         THEN `I may apply to the Administrative Review Tribunal, but it cannot review the Secretary's reduction for my debts to my employer (s 41)`
         ELSE `I may apply to the Administrative Review Tribunal for review of the decision made on the Secretary's review (s 40(1))`

§§ `s 34 -- what I must repay if I am paid later`

-- s 34(1): applies if the Commonwealth paid an advance and "an amount (the later amount) for an employment entitlement of
-- the person for which an amount was included in the advance is later paid by someone (the later payer)" to me or for
-- my benefit, and "(c) the later payer is not: (i) the Commonwealth; or (ii) the liquidator or bankruptcy trustee of the
-- employer; or (iii) the payee". (2): "There is a debt due by the person to the Commonwealth of the lesser of ... (a) the
-- later amount; (b) the difference between the advance and the sum of: (i) the amounts paid to the Commonwealth in the
-- winding up or bankruptcy of the employer because of Division 1; and (ii) the debts (if any) created by previous
-- operations of this section".
DECLARE `Who paid me later` IS ONE OF
    `the Commonwealth`
    `the liquidator or bankruptcy trustee`
    `the person who passed the advance on to me`
    `someone else, such as my employer, a director or a buyer of the business`

@export If I am paid later for an entitlement my advance covered, how much must I repay the Commonwealth (s 34)?
GIVEN `the advance` IS A NUMBER @desc The advance you were paid, in dollars
      `the later amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you were later paid for an entitlement the advance covered, in dollars
      `who paid me` IS A `Who paid me later` @desc Who paid you that later amount
      `what the Commonwealth has recovered in the winding up` IS A NUMBER @desc What has been paid to the Commonwealth in the winding up or bankruptcy because of the advance, in dollars, if you know (0 if not)
      `what I already owe under s 34` IS A NUMBER @desc Any debt you already owe the Commonwealth under s 34 for earlier later payments, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much must I repay` MEANS
    IF `who paid me` EQUALS `someone else, such as my employer, a director or a buyer of the business`
    THEN min `the later amount` (max 0 (`the advance` MINUS (`what the Commonwealth has recovered in the winding up` PLUS `what I already owe under s 34`)))
    ELSE 0
